Hey all.

I'm experiencing problems with IPTables and REDIRECTING, when i search 
around i find similar problems but no answers, i would be gratefull if 
anyone could shed some light on this one..

It's like iptables doesnt quite work when it comes to keep track of 
everything..

If I try a simple redirect to my webserver on the same host, port 5025 
-> 80 with
# iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -p tcp --dport 5025 -j REDIRECT --to-port 80

I would imagine this would do it

I can contact the webserver "fine" (http://pxysrv:5025)

apache access.log:
10.0.0.205 - - [01/Feb/2005:10:37:20 +0100] "GET / HTTP/1.1" 302 1084 
"-" "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; da-DK; rv:1.7.5) 
Gecko/20041118 Firefox/1.0"

But I do not get any reply from the server, but actually I do, it's 
messed up. When I'm sniffing the lan, I can see that it keeps resending 
with incorrent CHECKSUM, this is really weird i think.
And browser returns "Document Contains no data"

